# ROTATION-STATE - handoff rotation state (schema template)

Append-only. One row per handoff boundary. This template carries the fixed columns and an empty
state; it contains no live rows. Rotation law lives in the `protean-control-plane` procedure
skill; this file is the state half. Gate that reads it: `scripts/protean-ops/check-rotation.py`
(no two consecutive rows address the same next worker unless the later row carries an explicit,
non-empty exception reason).

Worker cells carry role names from `records/ROSTER.txt` only. Roles outside the roster are
rejected by the gate: the roster is the allowlist, so no other name list needs to be shipped.

## Columns (fixed)

| column | meaning |
|---|---|
| handoff id | `<project>-<boundary>`, unique per handoff |
| boundary time | UTC ISO-8601 when the handoff was made |
| previous worker | role finishing its assignment |
| next worker | role taking the next bounded unit |
| stage / unit | pipeline stage and the bounded artifact |
| capability justification | why the next worker owns this domain (capability and file ownership, never preference) |
| verified provider/model | read from the next worker's own configuration at dispatch, and confirmed after the run |
| exception reason | why the no-consecutive-assignment rule was waived, or `none` |
| release state | `active` while the handoff is open; `released <UTC>` once the next worker claims its lease; `blocked <reason>` if it stalls |

## Rows

| handoff id | boundary time | previous worker | next worker | stage / unit | capability justification | verified provider/model | exception reason | release state |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

The header above is the fixed column set, in the order `check-rotation.py` reads it.
Append one row per handoff boundary below it. A record with no handoff row yet is
not yet checkable: the gate reports missing input (exit 2), never a violation, until
the first row exists.
